# operating characteristics of the v1 success criteria (two-sided 95% Clopper-Pearson)

## False SUPPORTED: criterion 'upper bound <= T'
A calibrated two-sided test at alpha = 0.05 gives ~5% SUPPORTED on null datasets when the
metric is valid and judgment is resolved; requiring the effect in the pre-registered
direction halves that to ~2.5%.
  n= 200, T=0.07 (passes with at most 6/200): P(pass) — p=0.010: 1.00, p=0.025: 0.76, p=0.050: 0.12, p=0.075: 0.01, p=0.100: 0.00
  n= 200, T=0.10 (passes with at most 11/200): P(pass) — p=0.010: 1.00, p=0.025: 1.00, p=0.050: 0.70, p=0.075: 0.17, p=0.100: 0.02
  n=1000, T=0.07 (passes with at most 54/1000): P(pass) — p=0.010: 1.00, p=0.025: 1.00, p=0.050: 0.75, p=0.075: 0.01, p=0.100: 0.00
  n=1000, T=0.10 (passes with at most 81/1000): P(pass) — p=0.010: 1.00, p=0.025: 1.00, p=0.050: 1.00, p=0.075: 0.78, p=0.100: 0.02
  n=2000, T=0.07 (passes with at most 117/2000): P(pass) — p=0.010: 1.00, p=0.025: 1.00, p=0.050: 0.96, p=0.075: 0.00, p=0.100: 0.00
  n=2000, T=0.10 (passes with at most 173/2000): P(pass) — p=0.010: 1.00, p=0.025: 1.00, p=0.050: 1.00, p=0.075: 0.98, p=0.100: 0.02
  n=2750, T=0.07 (passes with at most 166/2750): P(pass) — p=0.010: 1.00, p=0.025: 1.00, p=0.050: 0.99, p=0.075: 0.00, p=0.100: 0.00
  n=2750, T=0.10 (passes with at most 244/2750): P(pass) — p=0.010: 1.00, p=0.025: 1.00, p=0.050: 1.00, p=0.075: 1.00, p=0.100: 0.02

